---
import ArticleLayout from '../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro';

const path = '/about/';
---

<ArticleLayout
  title="About Indian Broker Test"
  metaTitle="About - Indian Broker Test"
  description="Indian Broker Test is an independent editorial publication comparing Indian stock brokers using only verifiable published information."
  path={path}
  eyebrow="About"
  standfirst="An independent publication with one job: put the published facts about Indian brokers side by side, honestly."
  crumbs={[{ name: 'About', path }]}
>
  <p>
    Broker comparison in India has a data problem. Most "fastest broker" and "best broker" pages
    are written by brokers about themselves, filled with unverifiable superlatives, or padded with
    invented numbers to make tables look complete. Indian Broker Test exists to do the opposite:
    compare brokers only on what is actually published, cite the source for every figure, and
    write <span class="nd">Not Disclosed</span> - prominently - wherever the data simply does not
    exist.
  </p>
  <p>
    The site is static, fast, ad-free at launch (a sidebar slot is reserved for clearly labelled
    ads in future, and any advertising will never influence data or rankings), and carries no
    affiliate links. Rankings are computed from the dataset at build time; there is no mechanism
    to favour any broker, and no broker has any relationship with this publication. The full rules
    are in the <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Nothing on this site is investment advice. Investments in securities markets are subject to
    market risks; read all related documents carefully before investing, and verify every figure
    on the broker's official website before acting on it.
  </p>
</ArticleLayout>
